# 107 (found 2026-10-07 importing the suite's dynamicRef.json, G12
# phase 11): a mutual recursion residuates where a definition first
# meets itself, which depends on which declaration is unified first.
# Written with %k first, x is the residual and generation refuses it;
# written as below, x is one level of %k and generates. Both ports
# agree, so this is not a parity defect.
#
# expected: [aontu/recursion_unexpanded] at $.x, as with %k first
# actual:   {"x":{}}
%m = {b?: %k}
%k = {a?: %m}
x: %k
